      "description": "Career Services - University of the Ozarks Skip to main content Join us for Homecoming! October 15-18 Click here to check out the details! Ozarks Experience Ozarks Email Calendar Directory TSC Search Ozarks.edu: Narrow your search by content type Page Degrees Events News Offices & Services Faculty & Staff Links Menu University of the Ozarks Home Admissions & Aid Show sub-menu Learn about our admissions process, financial aid and begin your Ozarks journey. Admissions & Aid Costs & Aid How to Apply Visit Campus New Student Orientation & Move-In High School Juniors Incoming Freshman Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Calendar Apply Academics Show sub-menu Learn about our unique academic experience and the academic opportunities here at University of the Ozarks. Academics Our Academic Experience Degrees & Programs LENS Program Compass Study Abroad Library Canvas Student Success Center Jones Learning Center Faculty Directory Calendar Apply Life at Ozarks Show sub-menu Explore what makes life at Ozarks so special. Life at Ozarks Important Dates New Student Orientation & Move-In Student Engagement Residential Life & Housing Dining Shuttle Services Campus Recreation Spiritual Life Career Services Counseling Services Campus & Region Map Public Safety Title IX Calendar Apply Athletics Show sub-menu Our student-athletes strive for excellence on and off of the playing field, court or pool. Athletics Athletics Website Intercollegiate Sports Schedules Athlete Recruitment Eagle Tuesdays Fitness Facilities Support Athletics Recruit Me Support Show sub-menu Your gifts to University of the Ozarks truly matter to our students! Support Ways to Support Green Giving Update your info Grants and Initiatives Advancement Staff Hire an Eagle 1834 Society Planned Giving Give Bookstore Show sub-menu Our campus store located in Robson Library next to Campus Perks. Shop Now Conference Services Show sub-menu Ozarks offers a prime location for a variety of events. Contact us today to see how we can help make your next event a success. Conference Services Conferences and Meetings Weddings and Receptions Camps Catering Internal Events Contact Us! About Show sub-menu Learn about our thriving university, staff and history. About Leadership History Mission and Vision Our Christian Heritage Board of Trustees Rankings and Accreditations Student Outcomes Strategic Plan News Location & Directions Personnel Directory Offices & Services Marketing and Public Relations Reporting Calendar Request Info Search Ozarks.edu: Links Current Students Admitted Students Parents Faculty and Staff Alumni Search Request Info Visit Give Apply Home / Current Students / Career Services Career Services Blazing the Trail to Your Next Destination At University of the Ozarks, Career Services is your bridge. For students, it is the bridge between you and your first destination. We will coach you every step of the way through assessments, career exploration, networking, summer jobs, study abroad, internships, job search strategies, interviewing preparation, and graduate school applications. connect with our office First Destination & Career Profile ANNUAL Reports Career Tools for Ozarks Students: Handshake Check out jobs, events, and career videos. Handshake is where students and employers can connect! This platform is an Internship and Job database specifically designed for college students and recent graduates. Login by selecting Ozarks and using your student credentials to activate your account. Join Handshake Work Study Earn money that can go toward your student account while getting work experience – it’s a win/win! Jobs range from tutoring to office assistant to grounds keeping. Explore Opportunities Focus 2 FOCUS 2 CAREER guides students through a reliable, intuitive career & education decision making model to help them choose majors offered at Ozarks, explore occupations, & make informed career decisions.  Use access code Eagle to activate your free account. focus 2 assessment Skills Academy Ozarks Skills Academy is an online marketplace offering industry-recognized credentials and short-term certificates to equip students with in-demand skills. Designed for flexibility and aligned with workforce needs, the platform offers self-paced courses in fields like AI, project management, cybersecurity, and more. Explore more Internships Internships provide students with experiential learning activities in their specific major of study – exposing them to responsibilities in the workplace. It is important that students match an internship site to their career objectives. Internship Form Job Search Resources LinkedIn Job Board – Research openings, salaries, and employer contacts Glassdoor.com – Research company profiles, reviews, and salaries in addition to postings Indeed.com – One search, all jobs SimplyHired.com – Job openings, salary estimators, and more USAJobs.gov – Jobs in the US government GettingHired , Disability Job Exchange , and Inclusively – For candidates with disabilities seeking employment CareerOneStop – Explore the jobs, resumes, or training programs in your area Nonprofit Organizations Center for Nonprofit Management (Dallas/Fort Worth Nonprofit Jobs) Boys and Girls Clubs of America Goodwill Industries Make-A-Wish America Peace Corps AmeriCorps City Year Arkansas Sites Arkansas Democrat Gazette – Free Classifieds Arkansas Department of Workforce Services Jobs for the region of AR, OK, MO, and KS Little Rock Help Wanted Graduate Schools GradSchools U.S. News: Find the Best Grad Schools To access, follow the link and click “log on” on the right side of the page Section Menu Current Students Information Technology Emergency Alert Registration Career Services Work Study Title IX Event Submission & Publicity Start your Ozarks Journey Today Apply Now Career Services News More News Prev July 28, 2026 Job Placement for Grads Surpasses 90% for 10th Straight Year July 23, 2025 Job Placement Rate is 95 Percent for Class of 2024 June 10, 2024 Employment Success Rate at 95 Percent for 2023 Grads March 28, 2023 Bewley to Serve as Director of Career Services February 15, 2022 Senior Pasipanodya Aces Job-Search Test December 7, 2021 Thermozier Twins Continuing Life of Service October 26, 2021 Meet Your Alumni Board Members September 16, 2021 University to Present Career Fair on Sept. 23 October 9, 2020 Walton to Retire as Director of Career Services November 7, 2019 Career Fair set for Nov. 14 Next About last weekend 📦💜🦅🔁  We had a blast at New Stu FIRST DAY 📸 🔁   #uozarks #FDOC Classes are underway for our Fall 2026 semester an Welcome HOME, Eagles! New Student Move In & Orient Good morning, Ozarks 💜 How it feels to finally have our students arriving New Year, New Gear 👀🦅  @ozarksbookstore is stocked Us when we realize New Student Orientation & Move It’s Friday and 2 weeks until move in! How about s Three weeks from today, classes begin and our camp Follow #UOZARKS Facebook Instagram Snapchat Twitter University of the Ozarks 415 N. College Avenue Clarksville, AR 72830 1-800-264-8636 Contact Us Location & Directions Visit Apply Give Campus Directory Experience Ozarks Email Library Campus Map Public Safety Marketing and Public Relations Employment SARA/Online Students Complaint System Reporting Calendar Title IX Sitemap Accessibility Privacy Policy © Copyright 2026. University of the Ozarks is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission ."
